§ `Điều 1-3 — when the contract has effect`

-- Paid in full on signing, no agreed time: the period 1 June 2024 - 31 May 2025, both ends in.
#ASSERT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2024 9 1) `for` `a contract for a year from 1 June 2024, paid on signing`
#ASSERT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2025 5 31) `for` `a contract for a year from 1 June 2024, paid on signing`
#ASSERT NOT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2025 6 1) `for` `a contract for a year from 1 June 2024, paid on signing`
#ASSERT NOT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2024 5 31) `for` `a contract for a year from 1 June 2024, paid on signing`
-- Điều 2: never paid, no agreed time: no effect.
#ASSERT NOT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2024 9 1) `for` `a contract never paid, with no agreed time for payment`
-- Paid on 1 July with no agreed time: no effect on 15 June (fork F5), effect from 1 July.
#ASSERT NOT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2024 6 15) `for` `a contract paid on 1 July 2024, with no agreed time for payment`
#ASSERT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2024 7 1) `for` `a contract paid on 1 July 2024, with no agreed time for payment`
-- Điều 3.1: agreed for 15 June, unpaid: in effect up to 15 June, ended from 16 June.
#ASSERT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2024 6 15) `for` `a contract with payment agreed for 15 June 2024, never paid`
#ASSERT NOT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2024 6 16) `for` `a contract with payment agreed for 15 June 2024, never paid`
#ASSERT `art 3.1 — the day the contract ends for unpaid premium` `a contract with payment agreed for 15 June 2024, never paid` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2024 6 16)
#ASSERT `art 3.1 — the day the contract ends for unpaid premium` `a contract with payment agreed for 15 June 2024, paid on 10 June` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2024 9 1) `for` `a contract with payment agreed for 15 June 2024, paid on 10 June`
-- Tasco agreed the buyer may owe the premium: no termination.
#ASSERT `the contract has effect on` (YMD 2024 9 1) `for` `a contract with payment agreed for 15 June 2024, never paid, debt agreed`
#ASSERT `art 3.1 — the day the contract ends for unpaid premium` `a contract with payment agreed for 15 June 2024, never paid, debt agreed` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Điều 3 — refunds`

-- The 2025 contract: 365 days, 3,650,000 premium, 10,000 a day.
-- 3.1: ended on 11 January after 10 days, nothing paid: Tasco may demand 100,000; refunds 0.
#ASSERT `art 3.1 — the premium Tasco may demand` `a 2025 contract, premium 3,650,000, paid on signing` (YMD 2025 1 11) 0 EQUALS 100_000
#ASSERT `art 3.1 — the premium Tasco must refund` `a 2025 contract, premium 3,650,000, paid on signing` (YMD 2025 1 11) 0 FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Paid 3,650,000, ended after 10 days: refund 3,550,000; none if an insured event occurred.
#ASSERT `art 3.1 — the premium Tasco must refund` `a 2025 contract, premium 3,650,000, paid on signing` (YMD 2025 1 11) 3_650_000 FALSE EQUALS 3_550_000
#ASSERT `art 3.1 — the premium Tasco must refund` `a 2025 contract, premium 3,650,000, paid on signing` (YMD 2025 1 11) 3_650_000 TRUE EQUALS 0
-- 3.2: notice received 2 July 2025, 183 days to run. Owner terminates: 70% x 3,650,000 x 183/365
-- = 70% x 1,830,000 = 1,281,000; none after an insured event. Tasco terminates: 1,830,000.
#ASSERT `art 3.2 — the refund when the owner terminates` `a 2025 contract, premium 3,650,000, paid on signing` (YMD 2025 7 2) FALSE EQUALS 1_281_000
#ASSERT `art 3.2 — the refund when the owner terminates` `a 2025 contract, premium 3,650,000, paid on signing` (YMD 2025 7 2) TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `art 3.2 — the refund when Tasco terminates` `a 2025 contract, premium 3,650,000, paid on signing` (YMD 2025 7 2) EQUALS 1_830_000
#ASSERT `the day the contract ends on unilateral termination` (YMD 2025 7 2) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 2

-- The refund duties: in time on day 5 (3.1) and day 15 (3.2); late on day 6 and day 16.
#TRACE `art 3.1 — Tasco must settle the premium within 5 days of termination` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Tasco` DOES `refund the overpaid premium or demand the premium due` AT 5
#TRACE `art 3.1 — Tasco must settle the premium within 5 days of termination` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 6)
#TRACE `art 3.2 — Tasco must refund within 15 days of receiving the owner's notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Tasco` DOES `refund the premium for the remaining period` AT 15
#TRACE `art 3.2 — Tasco must refund within 15 days of its own notice` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 16)

§ `Điều 6 — transfer of ownership`

-- Transfer on 1 March 2025: notice by 16 March is in time (15 days), 17 March is not.
#ASSERT `Tasco was notified of the transfer in time` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 16))
#ASSERT NOT `Tasco was notified of the transfer in time` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 17))
#ASSERT NOT `Tasco was notified of the transfer in time` (YMD 2025 3 1) NOTHING
#ASSERT `art 6 — what the transfer does` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 16)) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it continues for the new owner from the transfer to the end of the period`
#ASSERT `art 6 — what the transfer does` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 17)) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it ends at the moment of the transfer`
#ASSERT `art 6 — what the transfer does` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 5)) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `it ends at the moment of the transfer`
#ASSERT REFUSED `art 6 — what the transfer does` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 5)) FALSE FALSE
-- 6.2 refunds: transfer on 2 July 2025, 183 days to run (as above).
#ASSERT `art 6.2 — the refund when the transfer ends the contract` `a 2025 contract, premium 3,650,000, paid on signing` (YMD 2025 7 2) TRUE FALSE EQUALS 1_281_000
#ASSERT `art 6.2 — the refund when the transfer ends the contract` `a 2025 contract, premium 3,650,000, paid on signing` (YMD 2025 7 2) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1_830_000
#TRACE `art 6 — the buyer or owner must notify Tasco of the transfer within 15 days` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 16)

§ `Điều 4, 5, 7 — duties`

-- 4.2.3: 15 days, 30 where Tasco verifies.
#ASSERT `art 4.2.3 — the days Tasco has to pay, from the complete file` FALSE EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `art 4.2.3 — the days Tasco has to pay, from the complete file` TRUE EQUALS 30
#TRACE `art 4.2.3 — Tasco must pay within 15 days, or 30 where it verifies` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Tasco` DOES `pay the compensation` AT 16
#TRACE `art 4.2.3 — Tasco must pay within 15 days, or 30 where it verifies` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Tasco` DOES `pay the compensation` AT 30
#TRACE `art 5.2.6.3 — the owner must give written notice of the loss within 5 days` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owner` DOES `notify Tasco of the loss in writing` AT 6
#TRACE `art 5.2.6.3 — the owner must give written notice of the loss within 5 days` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 6)
#TRACE `art 5.2.6.2 — the owner must not move, dismantle or repair without consent` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owner` DOES `move, dismantle or repair the damaged property` AT 1
#TRACE `art 5.2.6.2 — the owner must not move, dismantle or repair without consent` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owner` DOES `move, dismantle or repair the damaged property` AT 1
#TRACE `art 5.1.4 — the buyer may suspend the contract if Tasco refuses` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 100)
-- 7.3: the independent assessor's cost.
#ASSERT `art 7.3 — who pays for the independent assessment` TRUE EQUALS `the insured, the owner or the driver pays`
#ASSERT `art 7.3 — who pays for the independent assessment` FALSE EQUALS `Tasco pays`

§ `Điều 8-10 — claims`

-- Điều 8: physical damage, no police, no third party: 5 + 2 + 2 + 2 = 11 documents.
#ASSERT count (`art 8 — the documents the claim file may contain` `physical damage to the vehicle` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 11
-- Theft of the whole vehicle: 5 + 6 + 2 + 2 = 15. With police and a third party: + 5 + 2.
#ASSERT count (`art 8 — the documents the claim file may contain` `theft or robbery of the whole vehicle` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT count (`art 8 — the documents the claim file may contain` `physical damage to the vehicle` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 18
#ASSERT elem `the death certificate, and proof of lawful inheritance` (`art 8 — the documents the claim file may contain` `death of a person on the vehicle` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT elem `the death certificate, and proof of lawful inheritance` (`art 8 — the documents the claim file may contain` `injury to a person on the vehicle` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT elem `proof of the owner's compensation to the cargo owner` (`art 8 — the documents the claim file may contain` `liability for goods carried` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT elem `the scene diagram and photographs, if any` (`art 8 — the documents the claim file may contain` `physical damage to the vehicle` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT elem `the scene diagram and photographs, if any` (`art 8 — the documents the claim file may contain` `physical damage to the vehicle` FALSE FALSE)
-- Điều 9.1: alone 100,000,000; Tasco's 400 million of 1,000 million insured: 40,000,000.
#ASSERT `art 9.1 — Tasco's share where the policies overlap` 100_000_000 400_000_000 1_000_000_000 EQUALS 40_000_000
#ASSERT `art 9 — the insurers together pay no more than the actual damage` (LIST 40_000_000, 60_000_000) 100_000_000
#ASSERT NOT `art 9 — the insurers together pay no more than the actual damage` (LIST 40_000_000, 70_000_000) 100_000_000
-- Điều 10.1: an event on 1 September 2024: last day 1 September 2025; 10 obstacle days: 11 September.
#ASSERT `art 10.1 — the last day to claim, for an event on` (YMD 2024 9 1) `with` 0 EQUALS YMD 2025 9 1
#ASSERT `art 10.1 — the last day to claim, for an event on` (YMD 2024 9 1) `with` 10 EQUALS YMD 2025 9 11
#ASSERT `art 10.1 — still in time, for an event on` (YMD 2024 9 1) `with` 0 `, claiming on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT NOT `art 10.1 — still in time, for an event on` (YMD 2024 9 1) `with` 0 `, claiming on` (YMD 2025 9 2)
#ASSERT `art 10.1 — the last day to claim, for an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29) `with` 0 EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
-- Điều 10.2: decision received 1 July 2025: 90 days runs to 29 September.
#ASSERT `art 10.2 — a complaint about the decision received on` (YMD 2025 7 1) `is in time if made on` (YMD 2025 9 29)
#ASSERT NOT `art 10.2 — a complaint about the decision received on` (YMD 2025 7 1) `is in time if made on` (YMD 2025 9 30)
-- Điều 10.3: three years.
#ASSERT `art 10.3 — the last day to sue, for a dispute that arose on` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2028 1 15
#ASSERT `art 10.4 — the forum for a dispute that negotiation does not settle` EQUALS "a competent court in Vietnam"

§ `Điều 11 — the general exclusions, each with a case that fires it and a near miss`

#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `people only` TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `an intentional loss` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.1 intentional damage`
-- 11.1 inspection certificate: fires on the road; not off it; three causes of lapse spared.
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `a lapsed inspection certificate on the road` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.1 no valid inspection certificate`
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `a lapsed inspection certificate off the road` `people only` TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.1 — no valid inspection certificate in road traffic` `a certificate lapsed by tyres within specification`
#ASSERT `art 11.1 — no valid inspection certificate in road traffic` `a certificate lapsed by tyres outside specification`
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.1 — no valid inspection certificate in road traffic` `a certificate lapsed by a roof rack`
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.1 — no valid inspection certificate in road traffic` `a certificate lapsed by extra seats, 4 people on board`
#ASSERT `art 11.1 — no valid inspection certificate in road traffic` `a certificate lapsed by extra seats, 6 people on board`
-- 11.2 driver and licence.
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.2 — the driver's age or licence` `a sober licensed driver`
#ASSERT `art 11.2 — the driver's age or licence` `a driver with no licence`
#ASSERT `art 11.2 — the driver's age or licence` `a driver with a suspended licence`
#ASSERT `art 11.2 — the driver's age or licence` `a driver with an expired licence`
#ASSERT `art 11.2 — the driver's age or licence` `an under-age driver`
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.2 — the driver's age or licence` `a driver whose licence was lost in this accident`
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.2 — the driver's age or licence` `a driver whose licence awaits reissue`
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `an unlicensed driver on the road` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.2 driver's age or licence`
-- 11.3.
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `equipment operated without a permit` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.3 special equipment operated without a permit`
-- 11.4: damage to property only.
#ASSERT `art 11.4 — alcohol or drugs` `a drunk driver` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.4 — alcohol or drugs` `a drunk driver` FALSE
#ASSERT `art 11.4 — alcohol or drugs` `a driver on drugs` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.4 — alcohol or drugs` `a sober licensed driver` TRUE
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `a drunk driver on the road` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.4 alcohol or drugs`
-- 11.5, and the bus lane that 11.5 does not name.
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `a red light run` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.5 prohibited road or manoeuvre`
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `a bus lane entered` `people only` TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
-- 11.6-11.9.
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `a race` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.6 racing, unlawful towing or goods`
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `explosives carried` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.7 explosives or unlawful goods`
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `a loss in Laos` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.8 outside Vietnam`
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `a riot` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.9 war, terrorism, riot or explosives`
-- 11.10: by load for goods (1500 of 1000 = 50% fires; 1499 does not), by people for passengers
-- (8 of 5 = 60% fires; 7 of 5 = 40% does not), by the larger for both (10% and 60%).
#ASSERT `art 11.10 — overload of 50% or more` `a load 50% over` `goods only`
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.10 — overload of 50% or more` `a load 49.9% over` `goods only`
#ASSERT `art 11.10 — overload of 50% or more` `8 people where 5 are permitted` `people only`
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.10 — overload of 50% or more` `7 people where 5 are permitted` `people only`
#ASSERT `art 11.10 — overload of 50% or more` `a load 10% over with 8 people where 5 are permitted` `both goods and people`
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.10 — overload of 50% or more` `a load 10% over with 8 people where 5 are permitted` `goods only`
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `an overload of 50%` `goods only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.10 overload of 50% or more`
-- 11.11: 90 on 60 is 50% over and fires; 89 does not; no finding, nothing.
#ASSERT `art 11.11 — speed 50% or more over the limit` `90 on a 60 limit`
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.11 — speed 50% or more over the limit` `89 on a 60 limit`
#ASSERT NOT `art 11.11 — speed 50% or more over the limit` `no speed finding`
#ASSERT `art 11 — the general exclusions that apply` `speeding by 50%` `people only` TRUE EQUALS LIST `art 11.11 speed 50% or more over the limit`

§ `Điều 13 — reductions`

-- 13.1.1(a): no call and no written notice: 10%. A written notice on day 5 saves a missed call;
-- day 6 does not. No call to the police: 10%. Force majeure spares all.
#ASSERT `art 13.1.1(a) — late notice` `no call to Tasco, no written notice`
#ASSERT NOT `art 13.1.1(a) — late notice` `no call to Tasco, written notice on day 5`
#ASSERT `art 13.1.1(a) — late notice` `no call to Tasco, written notice on day 6`
#ASSERT `art 13.1.1(a) — late notice` `no call to the police`
#ASSERT NOT `art 13.1.1(a) — late notice` `no notice at all, under force majeure`
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `no call to Tasco, no written notice` `people only`) EQUALS 10%
-- 13.1.1(b), (c).
#ASSERT `art 13.1.1(b) — rescue and scene not secured` `the scene not secured`
#ASSERT NOT `art 13.1.1(b) — rescue and scene not secured` `the scene left only for safety`
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `a bus lane entered` `prompt and honest conduct` `people only`) EQUALS 10%
-- 13.1.2(a): the rate is Tasco's, within 20%-50%.
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `repaired without consent, Tasco chose 30%` `people only`) EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT REFUSED `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `repaired without consent, no rate chosen` `people only`) BECAUSE "art 13.1.2 leaves the rate between 20% and 50% to Tasco, and none was supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `repaired without consent, Tasco chose 60%` `people only`) BECAUSE "the rate supplied for art 13.1.2 is outside 20% to 50%"
#ASSERT NOT `art 13.1.2(a) — moved, dismantled or repaired without consent` `moved without consent, for safety`
-- 13.1.2(b): 72 on 60 in writing is 20% over; 71 is 18.3%; 72 not in writing does not count;
-- 90 is 50%, which is 11.11's exclusion and not this reduction.
#ASSERT `art 13.1.2(b) — speed 20% to under 50% over the limit` `72 on a 60 limit, in writing`
#ASSERT NOT `art 13.1.2(b) — speed 20% to under 50% over the limit` `71 on a 60 limit, in writing`
#ASSERT NOT `art 13.1.2(b) — speed 20% to under 50% over the limit` `72 on a 60 limit, not in writing`
#ASSERT NOT `art 13.1.2(b) — speed 20% to under 50% over the limit` `90 on a 60 limit`
-- 13.1.3: a rate within 50%-100%; and only where a third party is liable, for (a).
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `settled with the third party, Tasco chose 80%` `people only`) EQUALS 80%
#ASSERT NOT `art 13.1.3(a) — the right against the third party not preserved` `settled, but no third party is liable`
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `untruthful documents, Tasco chose 100%` `people only`) EQUALS 100%
-- 13.1.4: 30% over: the reduction is 30%; exactly 20% over: none.
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `an overload of 30%` `prompt and honest conduct` `goods only`) EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT NOT `art 13.1.4 — overload over 20% and under 50%` `a load 20% over` `goods only`
-- 13.1.5: 8,000,000 paid of 10,000,000 due: reduced to 80%, a reduction of 20%.
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `use misstated, 8 million paid of 10 million due` `people only`) EQUALS 20%
-- 13.2: late notice (10%) and moving without consent (30%) together: the higher, 30%.
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `no call to Tasco, no written notice, repaired without consent, Tasco chose 30%` `people only`) EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§ `Findings shown on the encoding`

-- X11: an event on 1 June 2024, Tasco's decision received 1 July 2025, a complaint on 1 August
-- 2025. In time under 10.2 (31 days), yet after the year of 10.1, which voids "every complaint".
#ASSERT `art 10.2 — a complaint about the decision received on` (YMD 2025 7 1) `is in time if made on` (YMD 2025 8 1)
#ASSERT NOT `art 10.1 — still in time, for an event on` (YMD 2024 6 1) `with` 0 `, claiming on` (YMD 2025 8 1)
-- X13: Tasco's three working days for an opinion ran out, the owner then dismantled: the 20%-50%
-- reduction still applies, at the rate Tasco chose.
#ASSERT `art 13.2 — the rate applied` (`art 13.1 — the reductions that apply` `ordinary circumstances on the road` `dismantled after Tasco's opinion was overdue, Tasco chose 20%` `people only`) EQUALS 20%
